From: Tim Michals <tcmichals@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 21:00:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH RFC v3 4/4] wifi: aic: fix SDIO V3 sleep status and PMU wakeup polling

On AIC8800D80 (V3 register map), the SDIO sleep/wakeup handshaking
registers and bitmask definitions differ from legacy V1/V2 chipsets:

1. Wakeup polling in aicwf_sdio_wakeup():
   In aic8800_bsp/aicsdio.c, wakeup polling correctly reads sleep_reg
   (SDIOWIFI_INTR_PENDING_REG_V3 at 0x01) and checks bit 4 (val & 0x10)
   indicating the chip PMU is awake. However, aic8800_fdrv/aicwf_sdio.c
   incorrectly polled wakeup_reg (0x02) checking (val & 0x1) == 0,
   which is the legacy V1 protocol. This caused aicwf_sdio_wakeup() in
   fdrv to repeatedly fail or time out on AIC8800D80.

2. Sleep request in aicwf_sdio_sleep_allow():
   For AIC8800D80 (!use_func2), sleep entry requires writing 0x10 to
   sleep_reg (0x01), matching the sequence executed by aic8800_bsp.
   Writing 0x02 to wakeup_reg failed to place the chip transceiver into
   the expected low-power state.

Align aicwf_sdio_wakeup() and aicwf_sdio_sleep_allow() in aic8800_fdrv
with the V3 SDIO register operations proven in aic8800_bsp.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A5E (Allwinner T527, AIC8800D80 SDIO Wi-Fi 6).

Signed-off-by: Tim Michals <tcmichals@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/aic/aic8800_fdrv/aicwf_sdio.c | 8 ++++----
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/aic/aic8800_fdrv/aicwf_sdio.c b/drivers/net/wireless/aic/aic8800_fdrv/aicwf_sdio.c
index ca2944b..d54a66c 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/aic/aic8800_fdrv/aicwf_sdio.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/aic/aic8800_fdrv/aicwf_sdio.c
@@ -1236,11 +1236,11 @@ int aicwf_sdio_wakeup(struct aic_sdio_dev *sdiodev)
 					u8 val;

 					ret = aicwf_sdio_readb(sdiodev,
-							       sdiodev->sdio_reg.wakeup_reg,
+							       sdiodev->sdio_reg.sleep_reg,
 							       &val);
 					if (ret < 0)
 						txrx_err("sdio wakeup read fail\n");
-					else if ((val & 0x1) == 0)
+					else if (val & 0x10)
 						break;
 					read_retry--;
 					usleep_range(50, 60);
@@ -1283,8 +1283,8 @@ int aicwf_sdio_sleep_allow(struct aic_sdio_dev *sdiodev)
 	    (int)(atomic_read(&sdiodev->rx_priv->rx_cnt) == 0)) {
 		AICWFDBG(LOGSDPWRC, "%s s\n", __func__);
 		if (!aic_sdio_hw->use_func2) {
-			if (aicwf_sdio_writeb(sdiodev, sdiodev->sdio_reg.wakeup_reg, 0x02) < 0)
-				sdio_err("reg:%d write failed!\n", sdiodev->sdio_reg.wakeup_reg);
+			if (aicwf_sdio_writeb(sdiodev, sdiodev->sdio_reg.sleep_reg, 0x10) < 0)
+				sdio_err("reg:%d write failed!\n", sdiodev->sdio_reg.sleep_reg);
 		} else {
 			if (aicwf_sdio_func2_writeb(sdiodev, sdiodev->sdio_reg.wakeup_reg, 0x2) < 0)
 				sdio_err("reg:%d write failed!\n", sdiodev->sdio_reg.wakeup_reg);
-- 
